{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_019HexosB5Cz4xgEj5ycHhor","type":"tool_result","content":"55\t           └── 001-ver.patch\n56\t\n57\tPackage YAML filenames use the canonicalized package name (lowercase,\n58\thyphens).  All three directories are configurable via CLI flags.\n59\t\n60\tMerge Order\n61\t-----------\n62\t\n63\tSettings are merged from least-specific to most-specific.  Later\n64\tlayers override earlier ones:\n65\t\n66\t.. code-block:: text\n67\t\n68\t   ┌──────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n69\t   │  1. Pydantic field defaults                      │\n70\t   │     (empty env, default build options, etc.)     │\n71\t   │                                                  │\n72\t   │  2. Global settings.yaml                         │\n73\t   │     (SBOM config, global changelog)              │\n74\t   │                                                  │\n75\t   │  3. Per-package YAML file                        │\n76\t   │     (env, resolver, build options, patches, ...) │\n77\t   │                                                  │\n78\t   │  4. Variant overrides (within package YAML)      │\n79\t   │     (env vars, pre_built, wheel_server_url)      │\n80\t   │                                                  │\n81\t   │  5. Version-specific patches and changelog       │\n82\t   │     (patches/<pkg>-<version>/, changelog entries)│\n83\t   │                                                  │\n84\t   │  6. Override plugin hooks (runtime)              │\n85\t   │     (update_extra_environ can mutate env vars)   │\n86\t   └──────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n87\t\n88\tFor environment variables specifically, the merge order within a\n89\tsingle ``get_extra_environ()`` call is: parallel-jobs settings, build\n90\tenvironment paths, package-level ``env``, then variant-level ``env``.\n91\tEntries can reference earlier values using ``$VAR`` template syntax.\n92\t\n93\tPackageBuildInfo Facade\n94\t-----------------------\n95\t\n96\t``PackageBuildInfo`` is the single interface the build pipeline uses to\n97\tquery all package configuration.  It wraps a ``PackageSettings`` and\n98\tadds variant awareness, patch discovery, and template resolution.\n99\t\n100\t.. list-table::\n101\t   :header-rows: 1\n102\t   :widths: 25 75\n103\t\n104\t   * - Category\n105\t     - What it provides\n106\t   * - **Identity**\n107\t     - Package name, variant, whether a config file exists, override\n108\t       plugin module\n109\t   * - **Resolution**\n110\t     - Sdist server URL, include wheels/sdists flags, platform\n111\t       filtering, per-package cooldown override\n112\t   * - **Build config**\n113\t     - Environment variables, parallel jobs, exclusive build flag,\n114\t       PEP 517 config settings, build directory"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f7fe830d-dbb0-435b-8ace-3596a0e40a72","uuid":"1e91b69d-e27a-489b-b07f-ddaf576952b0","timestamp":"2026-10-09T17:46:37.330Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/alustosa/git/model-routing-eval/.work/agent-eval/2026-10-09-claude-sonnet-5-5-effort-low-r1/cases/r05_fromager_version_prebuilt/docs/concepts/package-settings.rst","content":"           └── 001-ver.patch\n\nPackage YAML filenames use the canonicalized package name (lowercase,\nhyphens).  All three directories are configurable via CLI flags.\n\nMerge Order\n-----------\n\nSettings are merged from least-specific to most-specific.  Later\nlayers override earlier ones:\n\n.. code-block:: text\n\n   ┌──────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n   │  1. Pydantic field defaults                      │\n   │     (empty env, default build options, etc.)     │\n   │                                                  │\n   │  2. Global settings.yaml                         │\n   │     (SBOM config, global changelog)              │\n   │                                                  │\n   │  3. Per-package YAML file                        │\n   │     (env, resolver, build options, patches, ...) │\n   │                                                  │\n   │  4. Variant overrides (within package YAML)      │\n   │     (env vars, pre_built, wheel_server_url)      │\n   │                                                  │\n   │  5. Version-specific patches and changelog       │\n   │     (patches/<pkg>-<version>/, changelog entries)│\n   │                                                  │\n   │  6. Override plugin hooks (runtime)              │\n   │     (update_extra_environ can mutate env vars)   │\n   └──────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n\nFor environment variables specifically, the merge order within a\nsingle ``get_extra_environ()`` call is: parallel-jobs settings, build\nenvironment paths, package-level ``env``, then variant-level ``env``.\nEntries can reference earlier values using ``$VAR`` template syntax.\n\nPackageBuildInfo Facade\n-----------------------\n\n``PackageBuildInfo`` is the single interface the build pipeline uses to\nquery all package configuration.  It wraps a ``PackageSettings`` and\nadds variant awareness, patch discovery, and template resolution.\n\n.. list-table::\n   :header-rows: 1\n   :widths: 25 75\n\n   * - Category\n     - What it provides\n   * - **Identity**\n     - Package name, variant, whether a config file exists, override\n       plugin module\n   * - **Resolution**\n     - Sdist server URL, include wheels/sdists flags, platform\n       filtering, per-package cooldown override\n   * - **Build config**\n     - Environment variables, parallel jobs, exclusive build flag,\n       PEP 517 config settings, build directory","numLines":60,"startLine":55,"totalLines":126}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_019HexosB5Cz4xgEj5ycHhor","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Cfs5gmAx4KYEAzYEdnkrw","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01T3o5C8qbHBnT1eGBCZWQsy","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/home/alustosa/git/model-routing-eval/.work/agent-eval/2026-10-09-claude-sonnet-5-5-effort-low-r1/cases/r05_fromager_version_prebuilt/docs/concepts/hooks-and-overrides.rst","offset":40,"limit":40},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5180,"cache_read_input_tokens":94013,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5180},"output_tokens":40,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f7fe830d-dbb0-435b-8ace-3596a0e40a72","uuid":"dc687d26-f502-4a21-8311-3002c05f1d8b","timestamp":"2026-10-09T17:46:38.189Z","request_id":"req_011Cfs5gks6fP6GMeycTYXXn","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01T3o5C8qbHBnT1eGBCZWQsy":{"file_path":"/home/alustosa/git/model-routing-eval/.work/agent-eval/2026-10-09-claude-sonnet-5-5-effort-low-r1/cases/r05_fromager_version_prebuilt/docs/concepts/hooks-and-overrides.rst","offset":40,"limit":40}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01T3o5C8qbHBnT1eGBCZWQsy","type":"tool_result","content":"40\t     - Publishing wheels, validation, logging\n41\t\n42\tPer-Package Overrides\n43\t---------------------\n44\t\n45\tAn override module provides alternative implementations for specific\n46\tbuild steps.  Fromager looks up the module by the canonicalized package\n47\tname.  If the module defines the requested method, it is called instead\n48\tof the default; otherwise the default runs.\n49\t\n50\tOverride hooks cover resolution, source acquisition, building,\n51\tdependency extraction, and build environment customization.  Third-party\n52\tpackages register overrides via the ``fromager.project_overrides``\n53\tentry-point group in their ``pyproject.toml``, mapping a package name to\n54\ta Python module.\n55\t\n56\tSee :doc:`/reference/hooks` for the complete list of hooks and their\n57\targuments.\n58\t\n59\tGlobal Hooks\n60\t------------\n61\t\n62\tGlobal hooks are event callbacks that fire for every package.  All\n63\tregistered plugins for a hook are called sequentially.  They cannot\n64\talter the build result — they are purely side-effecting notifications.\n65\t\n66\t.. list-table::\n67\t   :header-rows: 1\n68\t   :widths: 25 75\n69\t\n70\t   * - Hook\n71\t     - When it fires\n72\t   * - ``post_build``\n73\t     - After a wheel is built from source (not for prebuilt wheels)\n74\t   * - ``prebuilt_wheel``\n75\t     - After a prebuilt wheel is downloaded (not built from source)\n76\t   * - ``post_bootstrap``\n77\t     - After a package is bootstrapped, before its install dependencies\n78\t       are processed\n79\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f7fe830d-dbb0-435b-8ace-3596a0e40a72","uuid":"68fee7d3-162e-465d-9d1e-1cee15d72ad5","timestamp":"2026-10-09T17:46:38.234Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/alustosa/git/model-routing-eval/.work/agent-eval/2026-10-09-claude-sonnet-5-5-effort-low-r1/cases/r05_fromager_version_prebuilt/docs/concepts/hooks-and-overrides.rst","content":"     - Publishing wheels, validation, logging\n\nPer-Package Overrides\n---------------------\n\nAn override module provides alternative implementations for specific\nbuild steps.  Fromager looks up the module by the canonicalized package\nname.  If the module defines the requested method, it is called instead\nof the default; otherwise the default runs.\n\nOverride hooks cover resolution, source acquisition, building,\ndependency extraction, and build environment customization.  Third-party\npackages register overrides via the ``fromager.project_overrides``\nentry-point group in their ``pyproject.toml``, mapping a package name to\na Python module.\n\nSee :doc:`/reference/hooks` for the complete list of hooks and their\narguments.\n\nGlobal Hooks\n------------\n\nGlobal hooks are event callbacks that fire for every package.  All\nregistered plugins for a hook are called sequentially.  They cannot\nalter the build result — they are purely side-effecting notifications.\n\n.. list-table::\n   :header-rows: 1\n   :widths: 25 75\n\n   * - Hook\n     - When it fires\n   * - ``post_build``\n     - After a wheel is built from source (not for prebuilt wheels)\n   * - ``prebuilt_wheel``\n     - After a prebuilt wheel is downloaded (not built from source)\n   * - ``post_bootstrap``\n     - After a package is bootstrapped, before its install dependencies\n       are processed\n","numLines":40,"startLine":40,"totalLines":85}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01T3o5C8qbHBnT1eGBCZWQsy","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Cfs5h3kqryHsR8qJ6xhcA","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01QVLXMyY1yC728myi1VeYYN","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /home/alustosa/git/model-routing-eval/.work/agent-eval/2026-10-09-claude-sonnet-5-5-effort-low-r1/cases/r05_fromager_version_prebuilt; python3 - <<'EOF' >/dev/null 2>&1\np='docs/concepts/package-settings.rst'\ns=open(p).read()\ns=s.replace('''PackageBuildInfo Facade\n-----------------------\n''','''Version-specific ``pre_built`` and ``wheel_server_url``\n-------------------------------------------------------\n\nEach variant can override ``pre_built`` and ``wheel_server_url`` for single\nversions under ``variants.<variant>.versions.<version>``.  The local version\nsegment is ignored, so a resolved ``2.8.0+cpu`` matches the key ``2.8.0``.\nA bare ``versions:`` key is treated as empty.  The bootstrapper's START phase\nre-resolves the download URL when the version-specific values differ from the\nvariant defaults.\n\n.. versionadded:: 0.95.0\n\nPackageBuildInfo Facade\n-----------------------\n''',1)\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\np='docs/concepts/hooks-and-overrides.rst'\ns=open(p).read()\ns=s.replace('''See :doc:`/reference/hooks` for the complete list''','''The ``is_pre_built(version, variant)`` hook is consulted only for a specific\nversion.  It returns ``True`` or ``False`` to decide, or ``None`` to defer to\nthe version-specific and variant YAML settings.  The local version segment is\nstripped before the hook is called.\n\n.. versionadded:: 0.95.0\n\nSee :doc:`/reference/hooks` for the complete list''',1)\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\n\np='tests/test_packagesettings.py'\ns=open(p).read()\ns+='''\n\ndef test_version_specific_lookup_ignores_local_version(\n    testdata_context: context.WorkContext,\n) -> None:\n    \"\"\"A local version segment does not hide version-specific settings.\"\"\"\n    pbi = testdata_context.settings.package_build_info(TEST_PKG)\n    assert pbi.is_pre_built(Version(\"2.9.0+cpu\")) is True\n    assert pbi.is_pre_built(Version(\"2.8.0+cpu\")) is False\n    assert pbi.get_wheel_server_url(Version(\"2.9.0+cpu\")) == (\n        \"https://mirror.test/simple\"\n    )\n\n\ndef test_is_pre_built_hook_only_called_with_version(\n    testdata_context: context.WorkContext,\n) -> None:\n    \"\"\"The hook wins over YAML, and is skipped without a version.\"\"\"\n    pbi = testdata_context.settings.package_build_info(TEST_PKG)\n    with mock.patch(\n        \"fromager.overrides.find_and_invoke\", return_value=True\n    ) as find_and_invoke:\n        assert pbi.is_pre_built() is False\n        assert pbi.pre_built is False\n        find_and_invoke.assert_not_called()\n        assert pbi.is_pre_built(Version(\"2.8.0+cpu\")) is True\n        find_and_invoke.assert_called_once()\n        assert find_and_invoke.call_args.kwargs == {\n            \"version\": Version(\"2.8.0\"),\n            \"variant\": \"cpu\",\n        }\n\n\ndef test_is_pre_built_hook_none_defers_to_yaml(\n    testdata_context: context.WorkContext,\n) -> None:\n    pbi = testdata_context.settings.package_build_info(TEST_PKG)\n    assert _pbi._default_is_pre_built(version=Version(\"2.9.0\"), variant=\"cpu\") is None\n    assert pbi.is_pre_built(Version(\"2.9.0\")) is True\n\n\n@pytest.mark.parametrize(\"value\", [None, \"\"])\ndef test_variant_info_bare_versions_key(value: str | None) -> None:\n    assert VariantInfo.model_validate({\"versions\": value}).versions == {}\n    assert VariantInfo.model_validate({}).versions == {}\n'''\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nEOF\nsed -n 1,40p tests/test_packagesettings.py | grep -n \"import\" ; grep -n \"get_wheel_server_urls\" tests/*.py | head -3"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1935,"cache_read_input_tokens":99193,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1935},"output_tokens":21,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f7fe830d-dbb0-435b-8ace-3596a0e40a72","uuid":"70e5291d-0c2c-4d0c-8e95-87ac8ae62707","timestamp":"2026-10-09T17:46:47.116Z","request_id":"req_011Cfs5h3VxcNxDJYtjG4Baw","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01QVLXMyY1yC728myi1VeYYN":{"command":"cd /home/alustosa/git/model-routing-eval/.work/agent-eval/2026-10-09-claude-sonnet-5-5-effort-low-r1/cases/r05_fromager_version_prebuilt; python3 - <<'EOF' >/dev/null 2>&1\np='docs/concepts/package-settings.rst'\ns=open(p).read()\ns=s.replace('''PackageBuildInfo Facade\n-----------------------\n''','''Version-specific ``pre_built`` and ``wheel_server_url``\n-------------------------------------------------------\n\nEach variant can override ``pre_built`` and ``wheel_server_url`` for single\nversions under ``variants.<variant>.versions.<version>``.  The local version\nsegment is ignored, so a resolved ``2.8.0+cpu`` matches the key ``2.8.0``.\nA bare ``versions:`` key is treated as empty.  The bootstrapper's START phase\nre-resolves the download URL when the version-specific values differ from the\nvariant defaults.\n\n.. versionadded:: 0.95.0\n\nPackageBuildInfo Facade\n-----------------------\n''',1)\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\np='docs/concepts/hooks-and-overrides.rst'\ns=open(p).read()\ns=s.replace('''See :doc:`/reference/hooks` for the complete list''','''The ``is_pre_built(version, variant)`` hook is consulted only for a specific\nversion.  It returns ``True`` or ``False`` to decide, or ``None`` to defer to\nthe version-specific and variant YAML settings.  The local version segment is\nstripped before the hook is called.\n\n.. versionadded:: 0.95.0\n\nSee :doc:`/reference/hooks` for the complete list''',1)\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\n\np='tests/test_packagesettings.py'\ns=open(p).read()\ns+='''\n\ndef test_version_specific_lookup_ignores_local_version(\n    testdata_context: context.WorkContext,\n) -> None:\n    \"\"\"A local version segment does not hide version-specific settings.\"\"\"\n    pbi = testdata_context.settings.package_build_info(TEST_PKG)\n    assert pbi.is_pre_built(Version(\"2.9.0+cpu\")) is True\n    assert pbi.is_pre_built(Version(\"2.8.0+cpu\")) is False\n    assert pbi.get_wheel_server_url(Version(\"2.9.0+cpu\")) == (\n        \"https://mirror.test/simple\"\n    )\n\n\ndef test_is_pre_built_hook_only_called_with_version(\n    testdata_context: context.WorkContext,\n) -> None:\n    \"\"\"The hook wins over YAML, and is skipped without a version.\"\"\"\n    pbi = testdata_context.settings.package_build_info(TEST_PKG)\n    with mock.patch(\n        \"fromager.overrides.find_and_invoke\", return_value=True\n    ) as find_and_invoke:\n        assert pbi.is_pre_built() is False\n        assert pbi.pre_built is False\n        find_and_invoke.assert_not_called()\n        assert pbi.is_pre_built(Version(\"2.8.0+cpu\")) is True\n        find_and_invoke.assert_called_once()\n        assert find_and_invoke.call_args.kwargs == {\n            \"version\": Version(\"2.8.0\"),\n            \"variant\": \"cpu\",\n        }\n\n\ndef test_is_pre_built_hook_none_defers_to_yaml(\n    testdata_context: context.WorkContext,\n) -> None:\n    pbi = testdata_context.settings.package_build_info(TEST_PKG)\n    assert _pbi._default_is_pre_built(version=Version(\"2.9.0\"), variant=\"cpu\") is None\n    assert pbi.is_pre_built(Version(\"2.9.0\")) is True\n\n\n@pytest.mark.parametrize(\"value\", [None, \"\"])\ndef test_variant_info_bare_versions_key(value: str | None) -> None:\n    assert VariantInfo.model_validate({\"versions\": value}).versions == {}\n    assert VariantInfo.model_validate({}).versions == {}\n'''\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nEOF\nsed -n 1,40p tests/test_packagesettings.py | grep -n \"import\" ; grep -n \"get_wheel_server_urls\" tests/*.py | head -3"}}}
