{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Cfs5kHxTGWdMZqW4nTug9","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The version-specific `pre_built` and `wheel_server_url` handling now works end to end. All 258 tests pass across `tests/test_packagesettings.py`, `tests/test_bootstrapper_iterative.py`, `tests/test_wheels.py` and `tests/test_bootstrap_requirement_resolver.py`.\n\n`ruff` and `mypy` aren't installed in `.venv`, so I haven't linted, formatted or type-checked anything. I haven't committed anything.\n\n- **`_pbi.py`**: `is_pre_built(version)` and `get_wheel_server_url(version)` now strip the local segment via `Version(version.public)`.\n  - `is_pre_built` calls the hook through `overrides.find_and_invoke` only when a version is given, using the new `_default_is_pre_built`. A non-None hook result wins over YAML.\n  - The `pre_built` and `wheel_server_url` properties now delegate to those methods with no version.\n  - The `versionadded` directives are bumped to 0.95.0.\n- **`_models.py`**: only the `versionadded` bump was needed. The bare `versions:` coercion to an empty mapping was already there.\n- **`wheels.get_wheel_server_urls`**: it already took `version`, so I didn't change it.\n- **`_start.py`**: added `_re_resolve_url(...)` as specified. In the START phase, the re-resolve runs before `add_to_graph` and the has-been-seen check. It logs at INFO before and keeps the original URL with a WARNING if re-resolution returns `None`.\n- **Source path**: the spec didn't say which sdist server to use for `pre_built=False`, so I used `resolver.PYPI_SERVER_URL`. `get_source_provider` still applies the package's own `resolver_sdist_server_url` override on top of it.\n- **Docs**: added sections in `docs/concepts/package-settings.rst` and `docs/concepts/hooks-and-overrides.rst`.\n- **Tests**:\n  - **`test_packagesettings.py`**: local-version stripping, the hook being skipped without a version and winning when called, the default hook deferring to YAML, and a bare `versions:` key.\n  - **`test_bootstrapper_iterative.py`**: the re-resolve triggers (pre-built flip, wheel-server change, none when unchanged), the graph storing the new URL, the warning fallback, a second parent of an already-seen package still getting its edge, and `_re_resolve_url` for the pre-built and source cases.\n- **Existing test changed**: `test_sets_pbi_pre_built_before_prepare_source` used a bare `Mock` for the build info, so its `wheel_server_url` values compared as unequal and triggered a re-resolve. I gave the mock explicit `wheel_server_url=None` and `get_wheel_server_url` returning `None`."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":7159,"cache_read_input_tokens":128919,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":7159},"output_tokens":787,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f7fe830d-dbb0-435b-8ace-3596a0e40a72","uuid":"1db7e537-75d2-4697-895f-f20eff0462a1","timestamp":"2026-10-09T17:47:29.548Z","request_id":"req_011Cfs5kHi4wV5zrDU9rxY1w"}
